[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://unitdecalcullmask"]

; Two identical floors under two identical decals. The ONE variable is the LEFT floor's
; `layers = 2` against a `cull_mask = 1048573` (0xFFFFD — every render layer but layer 2)
; on both decals: Godot draws a decal on an instance only where
; `decal.cull_mask & instance.layers` is non-zero, so the left checkerboard must vanish
; entirely while the right one — same decal, same box, same texture, default `layers` —
; is unchanged. Everything else is held equal: same mesh, same material, same box size,
; same albedo_mix, mirrored transforms.
;
; No other golden can witness this. unit-decal.tscn is the only other scene pairing a
; decal with a receiver and it uses cull_mask = 1048575, which excludes nothing, so a
; renderer that ignores cull_mask altogether renders it identically. The corpus scenes
; that DO mask (Truck Town's vehicles, the decals demo) are not visual-gated.
;
; Failure modes: cull_mask ignored → both floors carry the checkerboard, the left one
; wrongly. The mask inverted → the right floor loses its decal and the left keeps it.
; The layer test written as `===` rather than a bitwise AND → the right floor (layers
; unset, i.e. 1) fails against 1048573 and loses its decal too.
;
; The caption Label3Ds sit ABOVE y = 2.5, clear of both projection boxes. Inside one they
; are receivers like any other mesh and the checkerboard lands on the text — correct, but
; it buries the thing this scene exists to show.

